.TH hbpl1status 1 "${MODpage}" "hbpl1status ${MODver}"
#ifndef OLDGROFF
#include "macros.man"
#endif
'\"==========================================================================
'\"	MANUAL PAGE SOURCE
'\"==========================================================================
.SH NAME
hbpl1status \- report toner levels and state of an HBPLv1 printer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hbpl1status
.RB [ -c | -j ]
.RI [ device ]
.br
.B hbpl1status
.RB [ -c | -j ]
.B -s
.br
.B hbpl1status
.RB [ -c | -j ]
.B -i
.I device-id
.br
.B command2foo2hbpl1
.I job user title copies options
.RI [ file ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hbpl1status
reads the IEEE 1284 device ID of an HBPLv1 printer, such as the Dell 1250c,
and decodes its STS field: printer state, error code
and the levels of the four toner cartridges.
The printer updates this field live, so it can be read at any time.
.P
The device ID is read from a usblp
.I device
(Linux only, default
.BR /dev/usb/lp0 ),
from the CUPS backend through the side channel
.RB ( -s ),
or taken from the command line
.RB ( -i ).
.P
.B foo2hbpl1-wrapper
runs
.B "hbpl1status -s -c"
at the start of every CUPS job.
Installed as the CUPS filter
.BR command2foo2hbpl1 ,
it also answers the
.B ReportLevels
command, so the levels can be refreshed without printing:
.P
.nf
.ft CW
printf '#CUPS-COMMAND\\nReportLevels\\n' | lp -d printer
.ft P
.fi
.P
Levels are reported to CUPS as marker-levels, with marker-names,
marker-colors and marker-types, and the printer-state-reasons
toner-low-warning (below 15%), toner-empty-error,
marker-supply-missing-error, media-empty-error with media-needed,
and cover-open-error.
A missing cartridge has a level of -1.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B -c
Print CUPS "ATTR:" and "STATE:" messages on stderr.
.TP
.B -j
Print JSON on stdout.
.TP
.BI -i " device-id"
Decode this device ID string.
.TP
.B -s
Ask the CUPS backend for the device ID.
Only works from a CUPS filter or a program run by one.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
.ft CW
$ hbpl1status /dev/usb/lp0
Model:  1250c Color Printer
State:  0x11 0x05
Error:  none
Black Toner     80%
Cyan Toner     100%
Magenta Toner  100%
Yellow Toner   100%
STS:    00 00 11 05 00 ff 00 ff ...
.ft P
.fi
.SH NOTES
The STS layout was worked out on a Dell 1250c; see README.hbpl1status.
When the toner bytes do not look like that layout,
.B -c
reports nothing.
.SH FILES
.BR /usr/bin/hbpl1status ,
.B /usr/lib/cups/filter/command2foo2hbpl1
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR foo2hbpl1-wrapper (1),
.BR usb_printerid (1)
'\"
'\"
'\"
.em pdf_outline
